  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to fulfill; to grant; to make come true",
      "explanation": "To make a wish, dream, or hope become reality. Can describe both fulfilling one's own dreams and granting someone else's wishes."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "11807_kanaeru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{夢|ゆめ}を{叶|かな}えたい。",
      "english": "I want to make my dream come true.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "11807_kanaeru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{彼女|かのじょ}は{長年|ながねん}の{願|ねが}いを{叶|かな}えた。",
      "english": "She fulfilled her long-held wish.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "11807_kanaeru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{子|こ}どもの{頃|ころ}からの{夢|ゆめ}を{叶|かな}えるために、{毎日|まいにち}{努力|どりょく}を{続|つづ}けてきた。",
      "english": "I have continued to work hard every day in order to fulfill my childhood dream.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "{叶|かな}える means to make a wish, dream, or hope become reality through active effort or power.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pair: {叶|かな}う (intransitive — to come true, to be fulfilled)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{叶|かな}えている indicates an ongoing process of working to fulfill something, or the completed state of having fulfilled it.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {夢|ゆめ}を{叶|かな}える: to make a dream come true\n- {願|ねが}いを{叶|かな}える: to grant a wish\n- {望|のぞ}みを{叶|かな}える: to fulfill a desire\n- {希望|きぼう}を{叶|かな}える: to fulfill a hope\n\nUSAGE:\nVery common in inspirational and motivational contexts. The subject can be the person fulfilling their own dream or someone (including a deity) granting another's wish.",
